   "name": "Terminated capstan, as designed",
   "continuous": false,
   "output_rev": 0.15,
   "travel_m": 0.07539822368615504,
   "note": "3 working wraps at 20:1 is 0.15 output revolutions: the wheel turns 54\u00b0 and stops. Termination is the whole problem."
  },
  "B_round_loop": {
   "name": "Endless spliced loop, round groove",
   "continuous": true,
   "wrap_rad": 3.141592653589793,
   "F_tangential": 253.5346911217121,
   "T_tight_N": 1081.8448833680984,
   "T_slack_N": 828.3101922463864,
   "pretension_N": 955.0775378072424,
   "shaft_load_N": 1910.1550756144848,
   "rope_d_mm": 2.5,
   "mbl_N": 7300.0,
   "sf": 6.747732611419275,
   "r_drive_m": 0.01,
   "ratio": 12.0,
   "D_over_d": 8.0,
   "bends_per_km": 2859.289589435237,
   "loop_m": 1.0492116682006163,
   "note": "Works on a half wrap, but Dyneema's low friction on metal means the shafts carry a large pretension whenever the machine is switched on, load or no load, and the thick rope that tension needs forces a bigger drive pulley, which spends the ratio."
  },
  "C_vee_loop": {
   "name": "Endless loop in a 36\u00b0 wedge groove",
   "continuous": true,
   "wrap_rad": 3.141592653589793,
   "mu_effective": 0.27506577808748217,
   "F_tangential": 253.5346911217121,
   "T_tight_N": 438.1954532214714,
   "T_slack_N": 184.66076209975927,
   "pretension_N": 311.42810766061535,
   "shaft_load_N": 622.8562153212307,
   "rope_d_mm": 1.5,
   "mbl_N": 2628.0,
   "sf": 5.997323752859125,
   "r_drive_m": 0.006,
   "ratio": 20.0,
   "D_over_d": 8.0,
   "bends_per_km": 2885.430735812857,
   "loop_m": 1.0397061217811099,
   "creep_heat_W": 4.563624440190816,
   "rope_T_critical_C": 80.0,
   "note": "The wedge multiplies effective friction by 1/sin(beta/2). That cuts the shaft load 3.1x AND lets a thinner rope carry it, which lets a smaller pulley drive it, which raises the ratio from 12:1 to 20:1. This is the elevator traction sheave, which has done exactly this job for a century."
  },
  "D_toothed_belt": {
   "name": "Toothed belt (Gates 8MGT)",
   "continuous": true,
   "r_drive_m": 0.028,
   "ratio": 6.545454545454546,
   "stages_for_target": 2,
   "bends_per_km": 3403.8818960249046,
   "note": "Positive, no slip, no creep, and its tension member is cord: a toothed belt IS a cable drive that solved termination by moulding teeth on it and embedding the cord in elastomer, which is also what protects it. Capped at 6.5:1 per stage by the smallest stock sprocket."
  },
  "E_clutch_pair": {
   "name": "Two terminated capstans + one-way clutches",
   "continuous": true,
   "stroke_output_rev": 0.15,
   "strokes_per_km": 13262.911924324611,
   "note": "Keeps the termination, so it keeps no-slip and zero backlash, and the output turns forever. But every stroke is a full load reversal in the rope, the output torque pulses at the stroke rate, and reversing needs switchable clutches. Most parts, most failure modes."
  }
 },
